# Deliberately minimal.
#
# There is **no `* text=auto`** here, and that omission is the point: adding it
# would renormalise line endings across the whole tree in one commit, which on
# a repo several sessions write at once turns every open diff into a conflict.
# The rules below name individual files that break in specific, known ways.

# ── Gradle wrapper (S10-3a) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `gradlew` is a POSIX shell script executed by CI, which is Linux. Checked out
# with CRLF it fails as `bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M` — and this machine has
# `core.autocrlf=true`, so without this line that is exactly what a Windows
# checkout would commit back. Pinning it is what makes "reproducible from a
# clean clone" true on the platform that actually matters for it.
android/gradlew         text eol=lf
# The Windows launcher is the mirror case: cmd.exe needs CRLF.
android/gradlew.bat     text eol=crlf
# Never apply text filters to the wrapper jar. Git's binary detection would
# almost certainly get this right on its own; "almost certainly" is not a
# property worth relying on for the file that bootstraps every Android build.
*.jar                   binary
